A docker based test environment with three NSO nodes can be started easily:
  make start

NOTE! You might need to issue a "docker login containers.cisco.com" prior to this.
      1. Login to https://containers.cisco.com.
      2. Goto into your user and user settings.
      3. Click on "Generate Encrypted Passwod".
      4. Type your current password when asked.
      5. Copy the generated.
      6. Run "docker login containers.cisco.com" in a shell and provide
         your username and the encrypted password

      This downloads the needed containers from containers.cisco.com.


Network topology:

All IP addresses = 172.18.x.x

n1 (.1.2) ------ (.1.100) router (.2.100) ------ n2 (.2.2)
                    eth0          eth1     \---- n3 (.2.3)

The individual nodes can be access with a number of supporting makefile rules:
  make bash-n1
  make cli-n1
  make router

Run "make all" to see all available rules.


Ways to cause failures and make tailf-hcc and second-slave-ctrl take actions:
1. Kill NSO
  make bash-1
  pkill ncs
  ...
  ncs   # restarts NSO

2. Alter interface in router
  make bash-router
  ip link set dev eth0 down
  ...
  ip link set dev eth0 up
